genome.org/kb/downloads/#section_dosage')\n-   [Clinical Actionability](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/actionability)\n    -   [All Curations](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/actionability)\n    -   [Curations in Adult Context](https://actionability.clinicalgenome.org/ac/Adult/ui/summ)\n    -   [Curations in Pediatric Context](https://actionability.clinicalgenome.org/ac/Pediatric/ui/summ)\n    -   [Scoring Metric](https://www.clinicalgenome.org/docs/semi-quantitative-scoring-metric/)\n    \n    -   [File Downloads & APIs](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/downloads/#section_actionability)\n-   [Curated Variants](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/variant-pathogenicity/all)\n    -   [All Curations](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/variant-pathogenicity/all)\n    \n    -   [File Downloads & APIs](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/downloads#section_variant)\n-   [Statistics](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/reports/stats)\n-   [More](#)\n    -   [All Genes](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/genes)\n    -   [All Disease](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/conditions)\n    -   [All Drugs & Medications](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/drugs)\n    \n    -   [File Downloads & APIs](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/downloads)\n-   [](#)\n    -   [About ClinGen's Website](/tools/clingen-website-faq/)\n    -   [Learn About New Features](/docs/?doc-type=website-updates)\n    -   [How To Cite ClinGen](/tools/clingen-website-faq/how-to-cite/)\n    -   [External Data Attribution](/tools/clingen-website-faq/attribution/)\n    -   [Contact Us](/about/contact-clingen/)\n\n# Clinical Domain Working Groups\n\n[Back](https://www.clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/cardiovascular-cdwg/)\n\n## Hereditary Cardiovascular Disease Gene Curation Expert Panel\n\n[Affiliated to **Cardiovascular CDWG**](https://www.clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/cardiovascular-cdwg/)\n\n[Membership](#heading_membership)\n\n---\n\nThe Hereditary Cardiovascular Disease GCEP will function as a GCEP for genes asserted to be involved in cardiovascular diseases that are not currently being curated by any other GCEPs, including the existing cardiovascular disease GCEPs. Additionally, the Hereditary CVD GCEP will take on gene recuration of genes for dormant GCEPs in the CVD CDWG that do not otherwise have an intention to establish a recuration effort. The experts in the Hereditary CVD GCEP have an extensive knowledge of a range of cardiovascular disease, however, the experts will consult experts outside the group or invite additional experts to join the group should the need arise.\n\nThis group will:\n\n1.  Curate and review genes for CVD that do not currently come under the purview of another GCEP but for which there is a need for the curation to be completed and reviewed. Additionally, the HCVD GCEP will curate new genes that have more recently become important, such as FHOD3 for HCM.\n    \n2.  Complete the recuration of genes for dormant GCEPs in the CVD CDWG. The HCVD GCEP will start with recuration of HCM, Brugada, and HTAAD.\n\n[View all Gene-Disease Validity classifications approved by this GCEP.](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/affiliate/40104)\n\n#### Expert Panel Status *\\- Approved Expert Panel*\n\nStep 1\n\nStep 2\n\nDefine Group  \n*Complete*\n\nExpert Panel Approval  \n*Completed Aug. 2021*\n\n### Expert Panel Membership\n\nMembership spans many fields, including genetics, medical, academia, and industry.\n\n#### Chairs\n\n [![](/site/templates/resources/img/defaults/user_square.png ) **Jodie Ingles MPH, PhD**]( https://www.clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/ingles-11262 )\n\n#### Coordinators\n\n [![](/site/assets/files/11437/pwimg_tlt9la.600x600.jpeg ) **Emma Owens BSc**]( https://www.clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/owens-11437 )\n\n#### [Members (57)](#collapseMembersmembershipAccordion14132)\n\n [![](/site/templates/resources/img/defaults/user_square.png ) **Mhy-Lanie Adduru